In this modified version, we've added two new CSS properties: `filter` and `transform`. The `filter` property is used to apply a drop shadow with a blur effect, which helps to create a sense of depth and softens the edges of the circle. We've also added the `blur()` function to the `drop-shadow()` value, which specifies the amount of blurriness applied to the shadow (in this case, 10 pixels).

The `transform` property is used to move the element back by 10 pixels along the Z-axis (i.e., towards the viewer). This creates the illusion of depth and makes the circle appear to be more three-dimensional. By combining these effects, you should see a noticeable improvement in the perceived 3D-ness of your circle element!

