To further optimize the efficiency of finding unique words, you can use cellfun to apply the setdiff operation element-wise instead of using setdiff on concatenated cell arrays. This will reduce the memory usage and improve the speed for very large datasets:

```matlab
function uniqueWords = findUniqueWords(words1, words2)
    % Convert text to lowercase and split into words
    words1 = lower(strsplit(words1));
    words2 = lower(strsplit(words2));

    % Use cellfun to apply setdiff element-wise
    uniqueWords = {};
    for I = 1:size(words1, 1)
        uniqueWords{i} = setdiff(words1{i}, words2(:, i));
    end
end

% Call the function with your text data
