Here's an alternative implementation that follows the given formula for weighting helpfulness and verbosity:

```js
function generateNotification(notifObj) {
  let maxRating = -Infinity;
  let bestNotification = null;

  for (const [notifType, notifArr] of Object.entries(notifObj)) {
    let rating = 0;
    for (let I = 0; I < notifArr.length; i++) {
      const helpfulness = notifArr[i].helpfulness;
      const verbosity = notifArr[i].verbosity;
      rating += helpfulness * 94 + verbosity * 34;
    }

    if (rating > maxRating) {
      maxRating = rating;
      bestNotification = { notifType };
      for (let I = 0; I < notifArr.length; i++) {
        const message = notifArr[i].message;
        bestNotification[`${notifType}Message${i + 1}`] = message;
      }
    }
  }

  return bestNotification;
}
```

This function iterates through each type of notification in `notifObj`, calculates the weighted rating for each message using the given formula, and keeps track of the highest-rated notification and its corresponding messages. The resulting object contains the selected notification type as well as numbered message keys to avoid overwriting existing messages. This allows for the selection of multiple messages with different levels of importance based on their ratings.

